    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "```python\n    pointers = pointer + offs_m[:, None] * stride_m + offs_n[None, :] * stride_n\n```\n\nThe pointer addition does happen in 64-bit, but the overflow happens before that when you multiply the offset by the stride. That means it's your responsibility to upcast the strides to 64-bit if you need the extra range.\n\nClosing as not a bug.",
    "created_at": "2025-05-08T11:49:30Z",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/triton-lang/triton/issues/6748#issuecomment-2862761325",
