    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "Then there is another bug.\n\nIf you manually set the offsetting value to be a integral literal, the resulting pointer is still wrong.\n\nFor example, \nlet `offs_m[:, None] * stride_m + offs_n[None, :] * stride_n = 2257846272`, equivalent to `pointers = pointer + 2257846272`. \n\nBut this syntax will result in wrong pointer, which means triton doesn't handle that integral literal correctly, not like python (handled in 64-bit), nor C++ (handled in 32-bit).",
    "created_at": "2025-05-09T02:46:47Z",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/triton-lang/triton/issues/6748#issuecomment-2864933444",
